usage: audit_cleanup_causality.py [-h] catalog_cache text_cache output

Reproduce an eight-case cleanup/extractor contrast without changing product
code. From lcats/, project environment and PYTHONPATH=src: python
../experiments/10_gettenberg_qualification/scripts/audit_cleanup_causality.py
CATALOG_CACHE TEXT_CACHE /tmp/NEW_REPORT.json Requires the historical
gutenbergpy measurement environment, never a production requirement. Uses one
pinned historical parser and current local product modules; this is not a full
historical environment reconstruction. Both cleaners and both parsers receive
identical decoded text and current metadata. Source anchor intervals were
reviewed in an earlier run; exact interval retention is not literary approval,
and false can mean typography changes rather than missing narrative. Reads
eight cached gzip texts (32 MiB compressed/expanded each), archived evidence,
Git history and an existing catalog. Blocks socket creation during
catalog/source processing; no acquisition, cache setup or story publication.
POSIX alarm: 180s; Git subprocess timeout: 30s. Output must be a new path
outside repository/cache roots. Failures raise and produce no completed
output. Temporary historical module is removed. See results/gettenberg-scope-
audit-20261022/README.md for pins and interpretation.

positional arguments:
  catalog_cache
  text_cache
  output

options:
  -h, --help     show this help message and exit
